+# Hosting transition review
+
+Date: 2026-10-02. Revision: 1.
+
+## Adopted change
+
+The owner relaxed the allowed environment in [policy](policy.md) from local only
+to local or hosted, effective with revision 2. This removes the local-only
+guarantee. The [overview](overview.md) records that no application, database or
+hosting is implemented; readiness for hosted use remains open.
+
+## Impact assessment
+
+- Product, architecture and interfaces: hosting becomes an option. PostgreSQL,
+  the [retrieval scope](boundaries.md), model relationships and synthetic scenario
+  answers are unaffected. Application language and interface remain undecided.
+- Data and migrations: synthetic data and read-only retrieval remain required.
+  There is no implemented database or retained database state to migrate.
+- Identity, operations and recovery: intended users, exposure, access, hosting
+  design and service reliability remain undecided. They need a scoped review
+  before hosted use; no deployed service changes in this task.
+- Tests and release checks: the evidence here concerns documents. No existing
+  implementation machinery enforces local-only use, so none needs removal.
+- Docs and agent guidance: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) contained the repeated
+  local-only rule. It now directs readers to policy, removing that copy. Overview
+  and boundaries already link to policy. No other current consumer was found.
+
+## Open work before hosted use
+
+Owner: project owner, with technical reviewers to be assigned. Before hosted use,
+define the intended use and deployment design, then review the affected areas
+above. Record resulting requirements, responsible owners and acceptance checks.
+Completion depends on those decisions and passing evidence for the selected
+environment. This record holds that follow-up because no active hosting queue
+exists in the fixture. Implementation and operational verification remain outside
+this documentation task.
+
+## Evidence for this change
+
+Reviewed affected documents, searched current consumers of the environment rule
+and checked the documentation diff and changed-file links. The policy direction
+is adopted; hosted implementation and verified readiness remain open.
